-- allium: 3
--
-- pellucid-server: the server Pellucid will need once it stops borrowing
-- Pixelfed's. This file specifies behaviour: what an account, a post, a
-- follow, a token, a report and a federated delivery are and how each
-- changes. The rules name no language, no database and no framework;
-- section IMPLEMENTATION STATUS says what the code in this repository is
-- written in, which rules it carries out and what it leaves undone.
--
-- RELATION TO OTHER SPECS. pellucid.allium, in the .inference directory
-- of the pellucid repository, is the client. This file lived beside it
-- until 2026-11-10 and moved here with the first server code. The
-- client's contract PixelfedApi and contract Pagers list the
-- routes it calls; surface ClientApi here is the same set of operations
-- seen from the other side. Where this server deliberately differs from
-- Pixelfed, the difference is a decision below and the client spec's
-- KnownIssue that it closes is named.
--
-- THIS FILE IS CHECKED. `allium check .inference/pellucid-server.allium`
-- (allium 3.6.1) reports no errors and no warnings; one informational
-- note stays, that external entity RemoteServer has no governing spec,
-- which is true. Every lifecycle is a
-- field named status with a transition graph, which is the form the
-- checker's state analysis covers: it rejects a rule that makes a
-- transition the graph does not declare, a status no rule assigns and a
-- status no rule leaves.
--
-- STATUS OF THE DECISIONS. S1 to S4 restate what was asked for: a server
-- that does what Pixelfed's does, that existing clients and existing
-- instances can talk to, and that is less authoritarian. S5 to S16 are
-- proposals written to make "less authoritarian" concrete enough to
-- check. They are the author of this file's reading of that phrase, not
-- instructions received, and each one that is wrong should be struck.
-- S3's choice of language and S17 to S19 were taken by the same author on
-- 2026-11-10, while writing the first code, and S20 to S22 on 2026-11-12,
-- while writing likes, comments and notifications. They are proposals in
-- the same sense: the code follows them, and striking one means changing
-- code.
--
--   S1. PROTOCOL COMPATIBLE. The client API is the one pixelfed-rn and
--       Pellucid already speak (the Mastodon-shaped API with Pixelfed's
--       additions), so both work against this server unchanged. Between
--       servers it speaks ActivityPub with HTTP Signatures, so existing
--       Pixelfed and Mastodon instances federate with it.
--   S2. FEATURE PARITY FIRST. Accounts, photo and video posts with
--       albums, comments, likes, shares, bookmarks, follows with locked
--       accounts, blocks, mutes, hashtags, notifications, direct
--       messages, reports and moderation, search and discovery. Stories,
--       collections, groups and the import tools are not specified yet.
--   S3. NOT PHP; HASKELL. The server is written in Haskell on WAI and
--       Warp, with PostgreSQL, laid out as open-slop is. The language was
--       an open question in this file until 2026-11-10 and was settled
--       from Harry's stated preference for Haskell, not from an
--       instruction for this project. The rules below still name no
--       language, so striking this changes no rule.
--   S4. ONE SPEC PER SIDE. The client and the server each have a spec and
--       neither assumes how the other is built.
--
--   S5. MODERATION IS SEEN BY THE PERSON IT TOUCHES. Every action a
--       moderator takes against an account or a post creates a notice to
--       that account naming the action, the rule relied on and the
--       moderator's reason. There is no action without a notice: no
--       silent limiting, no hiding from feeds without telling the author.
--   S6. EVERY ACTION CAN BE APPEALED, ONCE, TO SOMEONE ELSE. An appeal is
--       decided by a moderator other than the one who acted. Where an
--       instance has one moderator the appeal is still recorded and
--       answered; the notice says who will read it.
--   S7. THE INSTANCE PUBLISHES WHAT ITS MODERATORS DO. Counts of actions
--       by kind and by month, and the list of blocked domains with the
--       stated reason, are public. No account is named in either.
--   S8. THE ACCOUNT BELONGS TO THE PERSON. An export of posts, media,
--       follows, blocks and bookmarks can be requested at any time and
--       does not depend on the account's standing: a suspended account
--       can still export and still move. Followers move with the account
--       (ActivityPub Move).
--   S9. LEAVING IS COMPLETE. A deletion the person asks for removes posts,
--       media, likes, follows and messages after a grace period in which
--       it can be withdrawn, and federates the deletion.
--   S10. FEEDS ARE CHRONOLOGICAL. The home timeline is the person's own
--        posts and the posts of the accounts and hashtags followed,
--        newest first, with nothing inserted and nothing reordered. Trending lists are computed from
--        public counts by a published rule and appear only where asked
--        for.
--   S11. A CLIENT CAN GIVE ITS TOKEN BACK. Public clients (PKCE, no
--        secret) are first class; a token can be revoked by the client
--        that holds it; a person can list and revoke every session.
--        Closes the client's KnownIssue no_token_revoke and its question
--        about the secret in the session file.
--   S12. ONE WAY TO PAGE. Every list pages by an opaque cursor in a Link
--        header whose rel="next" leads further into the list, for
--        everyone allowed to see the list. Closes the client's
--        likes_list_is_one_page_for_others and tag_feed_extra_request and
--        retires three of the four schemes its contract Pagers handles.
--   S13. UNUSED UPLOADS CAN BE TAKEN BACK. An upload not yet attached to a
--        post can be deleted by its owner, and is collected after a fixed
--        time otherwise. Closes the client's orphan_uploads.
--   S14. EDITS NAME WHAT THEY CHANGE. An edit changes only the fields it
--        sends; attachments are removed only by naming them. Pixelfed
--        deletes every attachment an edit's list leaves out, which is the
--        reason for the client's D30.
--   S15. OPERATORS ARE BOUND TOO. Direct messages are not readable
--        through any moderation surface unless a participant reports a
--        message, and then only the reported message and its neighbours.
--        Every operator and moderator action is written to an audit log
--        other moderators can read.
--   S16. NO TELEMETRY. The server sends nothing about its people to
--        anyone but the servers their posts are addressed to.
--   S17. THE SERVER GIVES ITS OWN NAME. nodeinfo's software.name is
--        pellucid. A server that is not Pixelfed does not say it is, and
--        the counts that crawlers build from nodeinfo stay true. The
--        cost falls on S1: pixelfed-rn refuses, in its own code, any
--        server whose nodeinfo name is not pixelfed, so it cannot sign
--        in here unchanged; and the Pellucid client's check_software
--        refused this server until 2026-11-11, when it began to accept
--        the name (KnownIssue client_refuses_this_server, recorded in
--        both specs). The client API itself stays compatible.
--   S18. A NEW SCHEMA. The database is this server's own, not Pixelfed's.
--        An existing Pixelfed instance would come across through an
--        importer, which is not written.
--   S19. WHAT IS STORED IS SCRUBBED, WITHOUT DECODING. An upload is walked
--        piece by piece, and every piece that is not needed to draw the
--        picture is left out before anything is written: EXIF with its
--        position and device, the embedded thumbnail, XMP, IPTC,
--        comments, and whatever follows the end of the image. A JPEG's
--        orientation is kept, alone. No image decoder runs on bytes a
--        stranger sent. A type that cannot be scrubbed this way is
--        refused. Thumbnails will need a decoder and are an open question
--        below.
--   S20. A NOTIFICATION LASTS AS LONG AS WHAT IT REPORTS. Taking back a
--        like removes the notice of it, unfollowing removes the notice
--        of the follow, deleting a comment removes the notice of it, and
--        deleting a post removes every notice about it. Nobody is told
--        of something that is no longer so, and liking and unliking in a
--        loop leaves one notice at most. Reading a page of notifications
--        is what marks them seen: the client API has no call for it.
--   S21. WHO LIKES A POST CAN BE READ BY WHOEVER CAN READ THE POST: the
--        whole list, paged the same way for every reader. Pixelfed gives
--        the list to the post's author and its first page to everyone
--        else. The post's entity names the latest liker to every reader
--        in both servers, so a like was never private, and a list that
--        stops after one page for some readers hides nothing.
--   S22. A COMMENT BELONGS TO THE THREAD OF ONE POST. It takes that
--        post's visibility and is read by whoever can read that post,
--        and by its own author. A comment can answer a comment, and the
--        thread is still the post's. Following a commenter opens no way
--        into a thread under someone else's followers-only post.
--        Deleting a post or a comment leaves what answered it in place,
--        as the posts of the people who wrote them. What answered a
--        deleted comment stays in the thread, which is where its author
--        can find it to delete it. What was under a deleted post is read
--        by its own author and by nobody else.
--
-- IMPLEMENTATION STATUS at 2026-11-12: the first batch of code, of
-- 2026-11-10, the deployment module that followed it, the page at the
-- server's own address, and likes, bookmarks, comments and
-- notifications. The code is in
-- this repository: Haskell (GHC2021), WAI and Warp, PostgreSQL through
-- postgresql-simple. The decision of each rule is a pure function under
-- src/Pellucid/Domain, named for the rule it carries out; the store
-- carries a decision out in one transaction; the HTTP layer is a route
-- table held as a value.
--
--   BUILT      Rules ClientRegistered, AuthorizationGranted, TokenIssued,
--              TokenRevoked, MediaTakenBack, MediaAttached, MediaReleased,
--              PostPublished, PostWithdrawn, FollowedOpenAccount,
--              FollowRequestedOfLockedAccount and Unfollowed. Since
--              2026-11-12 rules CommentPublished, PostLiked, PostUnliked,
--              PostBookmarked, PostUnbookmarked and NotificationSeen.
--              Rules CodeExpired and TokenExpired as a check made when a
--              code or a token is used. Invariants OneFollowPerPair,
--              NobodyFollowsThemselves, PublicClientsHoldNoSecret,
--              OneLikePerAccountAndPost, CommentsNameTheirThread,
--              NobodyIsToldOfTheirOwnAct, OneNoticePerLike and
--              OneNoticePerFollow as database constraints, with one
--              bookmark per account and post beside them;
--              PublicClientsAlwaysUsePkce,
--              AttachedMediaBelongsToItsPostsAuthor and
--              PostsHaveMediaAndCommentsNeedNone in the rules' decisions.
--              Contract ClientApiCompat's invariants SameEntityEverywhere
--              and ErrorsSayWhy for the routes that exist, and
--              OneWayToPage with max_id translated to a cursor; min_id and
--              page are accepted and ignored.
--              The reading rules can_see, for posts and for comments,
--              home timeline and public timeline, without blocks, mutes,
--              hashtags and limit_reach, none of which exists yet.
--              Surface SignIn's guarantee SecretsAreNeverReturnedTwice.
--              Decisions S12 and S13 for what exists; of S11, public
--              clients and a token given back by its holder, not the list
--              of a person's sessions; and S17 to S22.
--   PARTIAL    Rules MediaReceived, MediaProcessingStarted and
--              MediaProcessed run inside the upload request: the file is
--              scrubbed, then written, then its row is written once, as
--              ready. A file that cannot be scrubbed is refused and gets
--              no row, so status unusable is never reached. JPEG and PNG
--              are accepted; GIF, WebP and MP4 are in config's list and
--              are refused until each has a scrubber (KnownIssue
--              three_types_refused). Rule AccountRegistered exists for an
--              operator only, as a command: open_registration is false
--              and there is no route for it. Rules FollowRequestAccepted
--              and FollowRequestRejected have no route, and no route can
--              lock an account, so a follow request can be made only by
--              a test of the decision. The notices of a follow, a follow
--              request, a like and a comment are produced. A mention is
--              not: a caption is not read for names or for hashtags, and
--              a post's mentions and tags are sent empty. The
--              FederationQueued that several built rules also ensure is
--              not produced. The rules that would consult a block do not,
--              because no block can exist yet.
--   NOT BUILT  Everything else: the remaining account rules,
--              UnattachedMediaCollected, edits, shares, blocks, mutes,
--              hashtags, direct messages, reports, moderation, appeals,
--              federation, export, and surfaces ModerationDesk,
--              PublicRecord, Federation and Workers. No rule that is
--              built makes a notification of kind mentioned, shared,
--              tagged, message_received or moderation_notice.
--
--   ROUTES     GET / (a page for a person, surface SignIn).
--              GET /.well-known/nodeinfo, /api/nodeinfo/2.0.json,
--              /api/v1/instance, /api/v1.1/compose/settings.
--              POST /api/v1/apps. GET and POST /oauth/authorize.
--              POST /oauth/token, /oauth/revoke.
--              GET /api/v1/accounts/verify_credentials, /relationships,
--              /{id}, /{id}/statuses.
--              POST /api/v1/accounts/{id}/follow, /unfollow.
--              POST /api/v2/media, /api/v1/media.
--              PUT and DELETE /api/v1/media/{id}. GET /media/{file}.
--              POST /api/v1/statuses. GET and DELETE
--              /api/v1/statuses/{id}. GET /api/v1/statuses/{id}/context.
--              GET /api/v1/timelines/home, /public.
--              Since 2026-11-12: POST /api/v1/statuses with
--              in_reply_to_id (a comment). POST
--              /api/v1/statuses/{id}/favourite, /unfavourite, /bookmark,
--              /unbookmark. GET /api/v1/statuses/{id}/favourited_by.
--              GET /api/v1/favourites, /api/v1/bookmarks,
--              /api/v1/notifications.
--
--   CHECKED    74 tests: the rules' decisions as unit and property tests;
--              the scrubber against files built segment by segment; and
--              one session end to end through the WAI application
--              against a PostgreSQL started for the run (register, sign
--              in with PKCE, token, replay, upload, post, both timelines
--              with paging, follow, the reading rules, delete, revoke).
--              Where the work was written: GHC 9.4.7 with the library
--              versions nixpkgs' set provides, no warnings; and the
--              scrubber's output for a real baseline JPEG, a progressive
--              JPEG and a PNG, which an independent decoder read back to
--              the same pixels with no metadata left but the orientation.
--              On winsmuth, 2026-11-11: nix develop and the gate passed
--              with the flake's GHC 9.6.7, no warnings, all 74 tests.
--              The same day, where the work is written, every answer of a
--              two-account session against the running server
--              (registration, token, account, upload, post, the
--              timelines, relationships, compose settings, context) was
--              read by the client's own PureScript decoders and by its
--              Rust core's structs, with none refused.
--              Later that day, in the same place, the client itself
--              against this server at http://127.0.0.1:8080, which a
--              development build of the client now accepts (the
--              client's D34). Its core: sign-in through the consent
--              page, 25 uploads and posts, the home timeline in two
--              pages by cursor. Its desktop shell, the debug binary on a
--              display with no screen: sign-in from the login screen,
--              both feeds with their pictures, a profile, a follow, a
--              post's own screen. A like, Alerts and Explore drew this
--              server's 404, as routes that are not built should. A file
--              was not chosen in the client's composer, so no upload has
--              come from its webview.
--              2026-11-12: GET / is a step of the end-to-end session (a
--              page, the address in it, nothing that can run) and was
--              read from the running server; a path with no route still
--              answers 404 and POST / answers 405. Still 74 tests.
--              Later that day, 93 tests. The end-to-end session likes,
--              bookmarks, comments, answers a comment, reads both
--              threads and the notifications of two accounts, tries the
--              reading rules as a third account that follows nobody, and
--              deletes a comment and a liked post;
--              the decisions of the new rules have unit tests. Twelve
--              deliberate breaks of the new code were tried and eleven
--              were noticed. The twelfth, telling an author of the same
--              like twice, cannot happen while the index
--              notifications_one_per_like stands. A deleted post's likes
--              and bookmarks are removed and no test can see whether
--              they are, because nothing reads them afterwards. The
--              migration was applied to the database of the day before,
--              with its posts and follows, which read as before and
--              could be liked. Where the work is written, the client's
--              desktop shell against this server: a like, a bookmark and
--              a comment made in the app, the list of who likes a post,
--              and Alerts showing a follow, a comment and a like, with
--              the comment's notice opening its post. On winsmuth the
--              same day, as reported from there, the client signed in to
--              this server at http://127.0.0.1:8080.
--
--   DEPLOY     nix/module.nix, the flake's nixosModules.default:
--              services.pellucid-server.{enable, package, domain, title,
--              port, acme.{email, dnsProvider, environmentFile},
--              rateLimit.{perMinute, burst}, openFirewall}. The service
--              runs as its own user, listens on loopback, may talk to
--              this machine only, and reaches PostgreSQL over its socket
--              with no password. nginx terminates TLS with a certificate
--              by DNS-01 and limits, per address, requests to the sign-in
--              page and to client registration. The module was evaluated
--              for a whole machine against the locked nixpkgs with no
--              failed assertion and no warning. It has never run
--              (KnownIssue module_never_run).

------------------------------------------------------------
-- External Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Another server in the fediverse, as its actor documents and signed
-- requests describe it. Governed by ActivityPub and by that server.
external entity RemoteServer {
    domain: String
    shared_inbox: String?
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

value Bytes {}

-- RFC 7636, as the server sees it: the challenge arrives with the
-- authorization request, the verifier with the token request.
value PkceChallenge {
    challenge: String
    method: String
}

-- A rule of the instance, as its about page publishes it.
value InstanceRule {
    number: Integer
    text: String
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The client API, as pellucid.allium's PixelfedApi and Pagers call it.
-- One operation per group of routes; the routes themselves are the
-- client spec's.
contract ClientApiCompat {
    timelines: (viewer: Account, cursor: String) -> Bytes
    statuses: (viewer: Account, post: Post) -> Bytes
    accounts: (viewer: Account, account: Account) -> Bytes
    notifications: (viewer: Account, cursor: String) -> Bytes
    search: (viewer: Account, query: String) -> Bytes
    media: (viewer: Account, upload: Bytes) -> Bytes
    direct: (viewer: Account, other: Account) -> Bytes
    reports: (viewer: Account, reason: ReportReason) -> Bytes

    @invariant SameEntityEverywhere
        -- Every route that returns a post returns the same entity. The
        -- _pe flag is accepted and ignored: there is no second, stripped
        -- form to fall back to.

    @invariant OneWayToPage
        -- S12. A list response carries Link rel="next" while more exists
        -- and nothing otherwise; the cursor is opaque and is the only
        -- pagination parameter. max_id, min_id and page are accepted for
        -- old clients and translated.

    @invariant ErrorsSayWhy
        -- A refusal is a status code and a JSON body with error and
        -- error_code. A validation failure names the field and the limit.

    @guidance
        -- CORS: the API allows any origin for token-authenticated
        -- requests, so a browser client is possible. Pixelfed's default
        -- allows none, which is why Pellucid's requests come from Rust.
}

-- Server to server.
contract ActivityPub {
    deliver: (activity: Bytes, inbox: String) -> Boolean
    receive: (activity: Bytes, signature: String) -> Boolean
    fetch_actor: (uri: String) -> Bytes

    @invariant SignedBothWays
        -- Every delivery is signed with the sending actor's key and every
        -- inbound activity is verified against the key its actor
        -- publishes before it changes anything.

    @invariant AddressedOnly
        -- A post is delivered to the inboxes of its audience and nowhere
        -- else: followers for a followers-only post, the named recipients
        -- for a direct one (S16).
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

enum Visibility { public | unlisted | followers_only | direct }

enum ClientKind { public_client | confidential_client }

enum NotificationKind {
    followed | follow_requested | mentioned | shared | liked | commented
    | tagged | message_received | moderation_notice
}

enum ReportReason {
    spam | sensitive_content | abusive | underage | violence
    | copyright | impersonation | scam | terrorism
}

-- What a moderator can do. Ordered from least to most severe.
enum ActionKind {
    warn | mark_sensitive | remove_post | limit_reach | suspend_account
}

enum ActivityKind {
    create | update | delete | follow | accept | reject | undo
    | like | announce | block | move | flag
}

enum IssueStatus { open | closed }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A person's presence on this server, or a remote actor known to it.
entity Account {
    username: String
    -- Absent for an account that lives here.
    home: RemoteServer?
    display_name: String
    note: String
    locked: Boolean
    is_moderator: Boolean
    status: active | suspended | leaving | departed
    moved_to: Account?
    leaving_since: Timestamp when status = leaving

    posts: Post with author = this
    followers: Follow with target = this
    following: Follow with follower = this
    blocks: Block with blocker = this
    tokens: AccessToken with account = this
    notices: ModerationAction with subject = this

    transitions status {
        active -> suspended
        suspended -> active
        active -> leaving
        suspended -> leaving
        leaving -> active
        leaving -> departed
        terminal: departed
    }

    is_local: home = null
    accepted_followers: followers where status = following
}

entity OAuthClient {
    name: String
    kind: ClientKind
    redirect_uris: List<String>
    -- What the client may be granted. A consent can narrow it and
    -- cannot widen it.
    scopes: List<String>
    secret_hash: String?
    codes: AuthorizationCode with client = this
}

entity AuthorizationCode {
    client: OAuthClient
    account: Account
    redirect_uri: String
    scopes: List<String>
    pkce: PkceChallenge?
    issued_at: Timestamp
    status: issued | redeemed | stale

    transitions status {
        issued -> redeemed
        issued -> stale
        terminal: redeemed, stale
    }
}

entity AccessToken {
    client: OAuthClient
    account: Account
    scopes: List<String>
    issued_at: Timestamp
    status: valid | revoked | lapsed

    transitions status {
        valid -> revoked
        valid -> lapsed
        terminal: revoked, lapsed
    }
}

entity Media {
    owner: Account
    post: Post?
    mime: String
    size_bytes: Integer
    alt_text: String
    uploaded_at: Timestamp
    status: received | processing | ready | attached | unusable | purged

    transitions status {
        received -> processing
        processing -> ready
        processing -> unusable
        ready -> attached
        ready -> purged
        unusable -> purged
        attached -> purged
        terminal: purged
    }
}

entity Post {
    author: Account
    caption: String
    visibility: Visibility
    sensitive: Boolean
    spoiler_text: String
    comments_disabled: Boolean
    in_reply_to: Post?
    -- For a comment, the post at the top of its thread (S22).
    thread_top: Post?
    published_at: Timestamp
    edit_count: Integer
    status: published | withdrawn | taken_down

    media: Media with post = this
    likes: Like with post = this
    shares: Share with post = this
    bookmarks: Bookmark with post = this
    replies: Post with in_reply_to = this
    notices: Notification with post = this
    notices_of_it: Notification with comment = this

    transitions status {
        published -> withdrawn
        published -> taken_down
        taken_down -> published
        taken_down -> withdrawn
        terminal: withdrawn
    }

    is_comment: in_reply_to != null
    likes_count: likes.count
    shares_count: shares.count
    reply_count: (replies where status = published).count
}

entity Follow {
    follower: Account
    target: Account
    status: requested | following

    transitions status {
        requested -> following
        terminal: following
    }
}

entity Block {
    blocker: Account
    blocked: Account
}

entity Mute {
    muter: Account
    muted: Account
}

entity Like {
    account: Account
    post: Post
}

entity Share {
    account: Account
    post: Post
}

entity Bookmark {
    account: Account
    post: Post
}

entity Hashtag {
    name: String
    banned: Boolean
}

entity HashtagFollow {
    account: Account
    hashtag: Hashtag
}

entity Notification {
    recipient: Account
    actor: Account?
    kind: NotificationKind
    -- The post the notification is about: the one liked or commented on.
    post: Post?
    -- The comment itself, when the notification reports one. It is what
    -- the client API sends beside the notification, as Pixelfed does.
    comment: Post?
    created_at: Timestamp
    status: unread | seen

    transitions status {
        unread -> seen
        terminal: seen
    }
}

entity DirectMessage {
    sender: Account
    recipient: Account
    text: String
    sent_at: Timestamp
    status: sent | unsent

    transitions status {
        sent -> unsent
        terminal: unsent
    }
}

entity Report {
    reporter: Account
    reason: ReportReason
    note: String
    about_post: Post?
    about_account: Account
    about_message: DirectMessage?
    filed_at: Timestamp
    status: filed | actioned | dismissed

    transitions status {
        filed -> actioned
        filed -> dismissed
        terminal: actioned, dismissed
    }
}

-- One thing a moderator did, and the notice of it (S5). The notice is not
-- a separate entity so that an action cannot exist without one.
entity ModerationAction {
    kind: ActionKind
    subject: Account
    post: Post?
    moderator: Account
    rule_cited: InstanceRule
    reason: String
    report: Report?
    taken_at: Timestamp
    appeal_text: String?
    decided_by: Account?
    status: applied | under_appeal | upheld | reversed

    transitions status {
        applied -> under_appeal
        under_appeal -> upheld
        under_appeal -> reversed
        terminal: upheld, reversed
    }
}

-- One line of the audit log (S15).
entity AuditEntry {
    actor: Account
    what: String
    at: Timestamp
}

entity DomainBlock {
    domain: String
    reason: String
    blocked_by: Account
}

-- One activity on its way to one remote inbox.
entity Delivery {
    kind: ActivityKind
    from: Account
    inbox: String
    attempts: Integer
    next_attempt_at: Timestamp
    status: queued | delivered | backing_off | abandoned

    transitions status {
        queued -> delivered
        queued -> backing_off
        backing_off -> delivered
        backing_off -> queued
        backing_off -> abandoned
        terminal: delivered, abandoned
    }
}

-- One activity received from a remote server.
entity InboundActivity {
    kind: ActivityKind
    origin: RemoteServer
    actor_uri: String
    status: awaiting_verification | accepted | refused

    transitions status {
        awaiting_verification -> accepted
        awaiting_verification -> refused
        terminal: accepted, refused
    }
}

-- Something the code is known to do wrong or not to do, where the spec
-- says otherwise or an operator would assume otherwise.
entity KnownIssue {
    name: String
    status: IssueStatus
    effect: String
    closes_when: String
}

-- A person's copy of everything they put here (S8).
entity Export {
    account: Account
    requested_at: Timestamp
    built_at: Timestamp when status = built
    status: asked | built | cleared

    transitions status {
        asked -> built
        built -> cleared
        terminal: cleared
    }
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    -- Published at the instance endpoint so a client can apply them first.
    max_caption_length: Integer = 500
    max_album_length: Integer = 10
    max_alt_text_length: Integer = 1000
    max_spoiler_length: Integer = 140
    max_message_length: Integer = 2000
    max_report_note_length: Integer = 255
    max_edits_per_post: Integer = 10
    max_upload_kb: Integer = 15000
    allowed_media_types: List<String> = [ "image/jpeg", "image/png", "image/gif", "image/webp", "video/mp4" ]
    open_registration: Boolean = false
    authorization_code_lifetime: Duration = 10.minutes
    access_token_lifetime: Duration = 365.days
    unattached_media_lifetime: Duration = 24.hours
    deletion_grace: Duration = 14.days
    export_lifetime: Duration = 7.days
    delivery_max_attempts: Integer = 8
    delivery_first_backoff: Duration = 1.minute
    list_page: Integer = 20
    list_page_max: Integer = 40
    -- How many comments one request for a thread returns, oldest first.
    context_max: Integer = 100
    -- The longest side of a picture, in pixels. The server does not
    -- decode an upload, but every client that shows it will.
    max_image_side: Integer = 16384
}

default KnownIssue no_sign_in_throttle = {
    name: "the server itself limits nothing: not password guesses, not anything else asked",
    status: open,
    effect: "the NixOS module's proxy limits requests per address to the sign-in page and to client registration, which slows one address and does nothing about many; a server run without that proxy has no limit at all. The consent page checks a password on every request. Each check costs one Argon2id computation, the answer for an unknown name takes as long as for a wrong password, and a password is at least twelve characters; beyond that an attacker can try as often as the machine allows, and enough parallel attempts will also exhaust its memory. No other route is limited either: registering a client needs no token and writes a row each time",
    closes_when: "failed sign-ins are counted per account and per address, further attempts are delayed or refused past a limit, the person is told, and requests without a token are limited per address. Must close before the server faces the internet"
}

default KnownIssue three_types_refused = {
    name: "GIF, WebP and MP4 uploads are refused",
    status: open,
    effect: "config.allowed_media_types lists five types and the code accepts two, JPEG and PNG, because S19 forbids storing what has not been scrubbed and only those two have a scrubber. A video cannot be posted at all",
    closes_when: "each of the three has a scrubber with tests against real files, and the code's list equals the config's"
}

default KnownIssue no_thumbnails = {
    name: "preview_url is the full file",
    status: open,
    effect: "no smaller rendition is made, so a grid of posts downloads every picture at full size, and blurhash is null",
    closes_when: "the open question on decoding is answered and previews are generated under it"
}

default KnownIssue timers_run_only_at_use = {
    name: "nothing in the server runs on a clock",
    status: open,
    effect: "rules CodeExpired and TokenExpired are applied when a code or a token is presented, which gives the right answers, but a row nobody presents again keeps its old status. Rule UnattachedMediaCollected never runs: an upload that is never posted and never taken back stays on disk",
    closes_when: "a worker applies the three temporal rules on a schedule"
}

default KnownIssue uploads_held_in_memory = {
    name: "an upload is read into memory whole",
    status: open,
    effect: "each upload in flight holds up to max_upload_kb twice, as received and as scrubbed. A handful of clients uploading together can use several hundred megabytes",
    closes_when: "the body is spooled to a temporary file and scrubbed from there, or concurrent uploads are bounded"
}

default KnownIssue ids_within_one_millisecond = {
    name: "two ids made in the same millisecond can sort against their order of creation",
    status: open,
    effect: "an id is a millisecond count and a sixteen-bit counter. When the counter wraps inside one millisecond the later row gets the smaller id, so the two sit in a list in the wrong order relative to each other. Ids stay unique and every list stays a consistent order",
    closes_when: "the id function waits for the next millisecond when its counter wraps, or the ordering is accepted and this entry is closed with that decision"
}

default KnownIssue client_refuses_this_server = {
    name: "the Pellucid client has not signed in to this server",
    status: open,
    effect: "the client's check_software accepts the name pellucid (S17), and since 2026-11-11 a development build of the client reaches a server on its own machine over http://127.0.0.1 (the client's D34). On 2026-11-12 the client signed in to this server on winsmuth, as reported from there. What is left: whether a photo chosen in the client's composer on winsmuth reaches this server has not been reported, and a release build of the client, which is https only, trusts the public certificate authorities and no others, needs a deployed server, of which there is none",
    closes_when: "a session from the client against a deployed server has signed in, posted a photo and read it back"
}

default KnownIssue module_never_run = {
    name: "the NixOS module has been evaluated and never run",
    status: open,
    effect: "whether the service starts under the module's systemd restrictions, whether nginx accepts the configuration, whether the certificate is issued, and whether the database role is recognised over the socket have not been seen. nix flake check, which runs the test suite inside the build sandbox, has not been run either",
    closes_when: "the service has run on blade under the module with a certificate issued, pellucid-server-manage has created an account there, and nix flake check has passed on winsmuth"
}

default KnownIssue flake_unbuilt = {
    name: "the flake had been evaluated and never built",
    status: closed,
    effect: "the code was first compiled and tested with GHC 9.4.7, and the flake pins 9.6.7",
    closes_when: "Closed 2026-11-11: nix develop and the gate in scripts/check.fish passed on winsmuth with GHC 9.6.7, no warnings, 74 tests. nix flake check moved to module_never_run"
}

default KnownIssue code_unformatted = {
    name: "the delivered code was not in fourmolu's layout",
    status: closed,
    effect: "the files of the first batch were sent as written. fourmolu 0.15.0.0, the version the flake provides, rewrote 34 of the 39 with the repository's fourmolu.yaml. The gate checks formatting from 2026-11-11",
    closes_when: "Closed 2026-11-11: fourmolu --mode inplace app src test was run on winsmuth and the gate passed, its format check included"
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Accounts ---------------------------------------------------------------

rule AccountRegistered {
    when: RegistrationSubmitted(_, username, password)
    requires: config.open_registration
    requires: not exists Account{username: username, home: null}
    ensures: Account.created(username: username, display_name: username, note: "", locked: false, is_moderator: false, status: active)

    @guidance
        -- The password is stored only as a slow salted hash. Usernames are
        -- compared without case. When registration is closed an operator
        -- creates accounts; nothing else about them differs.
}

rule DeletionRequested {
    when: DeletionRequested(account)
    requires: account.status = active or account.status = suspended
    ensures:
        account.status = leaving
        account.leaving_since = now

    @guidance
        -- S9. Suspension does not take away the right to leave.
}

rule DeletionWithdrawn {
    when: DeletionWithdrawn(account)
    requires: account.status = leaving
    ensures:
        account.status = active
        account.leaving_since = null
}

rule AccountDeparted {
    when: account: Account.leaving_since + config.deletion_grace <= now
    requires: account.status = leaving
    ensures:
        account.status = departed
        for post in account.posts where status = published:
            post.status = withdrawn
        for follow in account.followers:
            not exists follow
        for follow in account.following:
            not exists follow
        for token in account.tokens where status = valid:
            token.status = revoked
        FederationQueued(kind: delete, from: account)

    @guidance
        -- Media, likes, bookmarks, messages and notifications of the
        -- account are removed with it. The username is not reissued.
}

rule AccountSuspended {
    when: action: ModerationAction.created
    requires: action.kind = suspend_account
    requires: action.subject.status = active
    ensures: action.subject.status = suspended
}

rule AccountReinstated {
    when: action: ModerationAction.status transitions_to reversed
    requires: action.kind = suspend_account
    requires: action.subject.status = suspended
    ensures: action.subject.status = active
}

rule AccountMoved {
    when: MoveRequested(account, destination)
    requires: account.status = active or account.status = suspended
    requires: account.moved_to = null
    requires: aliases_include(destination, account)
    ensures:
        account.moved_to = destination
        FederationQueued(kind: move, from: account)

    @guidance
        -- S8. The destination must name this account as an alias first,
        -- which is what stops one account from moving another's
        -- followers. Followers on this server follow the destination at
        -- once; remote ones act on the Move they receive.
}

-- OAuth ------------------------------------------------------------------

rule ClientRegistered {
    when: ClientRegistrationSubmitted(_, name, kind, redirect_uris, scopes)
    requires: redirect_uris != []
    requires: scopes != []
    ensures: OAuthClient.created(name: name, kind: kind, redirect_uris: redirect_uris, scopes: scopes)

    @guidance
        -- A confidential client also receives a secret, shown once and
        -- stored hashed. A public client has none (S11).
}

rule AuthorizationGranted {
    when: ConsentGiven(account, client, redirect_uri, scopes, pkce)
    requires: account.status = active or account.status = suspended
    requires: redirect_uri in client.redirect_uris
    requires: scopes != [] and scopes.all(s => s in client.scopes)
    requires: client.kind = confidential_client or pkce != null
    ensures: AuthorizationCode.created(client: client, account: account, redirect_uri: redirect_uri, scopes: scopes, pkce: pkce, issued_at: now, status: issued)

    @guidance
        -- A public client without a challenge is refused at the consent
        -- page. Only S256 is accepted as the method.
}

rule TokenIssued {
    when: CodePresented(client, code, redirect_uri, verifier, secret)
    requires: code.client = client
    requires: code.status = issued
    requires: redirect_uri = code.redirect_uri
    requires: code.pkce = null or challenge_matches(code.pkce, verifier)
    requires: code.client.kind = public_client or secret_matches(code.client, secret)
    ensures:
        code.status = redeemed
        AccessToken.created(client: code.client, account: code.account, scopes: code.scopes, issued_at: now, status: valid)

    @guidance
        -- A code is redeemed once. Presenting a redeemed code again
        -- revokes the token it produced, since one of the two presenters
        -- stole it.
}

rule CodeExpired {
    when: code: AuthorizationCode.issued_at + config.authorization_code_lifetime <= now
    requires: code.status = issued
    ensures: code.status = stale
}

rule TokenRevoked {
    when: RevocationRequested(account, token)
    requires: token.status = valid
    requires: token.account = account
    ensures: token.status = revoked

    @guidance
        -- RFC 7009 for the client holding the token, and the same effect
        -- from the person's list of sessions (S11). Revoking is allowed
        -- with the very token being revoked.
}

rule TokenExpired {
    when: token: AccessToken.issued_at + config.access_token_lifetime <= now
    requires: token.status = valid
    ensures: token.status = lapsed
}

-- Media ------------------------------------------------------------------

rule MediaReceived {
    when: UploadSubmitted(account, mime, size_bytes)
    requires: account.status = active
    requires: mime in config.allowed_media_types
    requires: size_bytes > 0 and size_bytes <= config.max_upload_kb * 1024
    ensures: Media.created(owner: account, mime: mime, size_bytes: size_bytes, alt_text: "", uploaded_at: now, status: received)
}

rule MediaProcessingStarted {
    when: media: Media.created
    requires: media.status = received
    ensures: media.status = processing

    @guidance
        -- The type is decided by the content, not by the declared MIME
        -- type. Metadata that locates the person (EXIF position, device
        -- serial) is stripped before anything is stored for serving
        -- (S19). A picture with a side longer than config.max_image_side,
        -- and a file that ends before its image does, fail processing.
}

rule MediaProcessed {
    when: ProcessingFinished(media)
    requires: media.status = processing
    ensures: media.status = ready
}

rule MediaProcessingFailed {
    when: ProcessingFailed(media)
    requires: media.status = processing
    ensures: media.status = unusable
}

rule MediaTakenBack {
    when: MediaDeleteRequested(account, media)
    requires: media.owner = account
    requires: media.status = ready or media.status = unusable
    ensures: media.status = purged

    @guidance
        -- S13. Only before the media is attached; afterwards it leaves
        -- with its post or by an edit that names it.
}

rule UnattachedMediaCollected {
    when: media: Media.uploaded_at + config.unattached_media_lifetime <= now
    requires: media.status = ready or media.status = unusable
    ensures: media.status = purged
}

rule MediaAttached {
    when: AttachRequested(media, post)
    requires: media.status = ready
    ensures:
        media.status = attached
        media.post = post

    @guidance
        -- Emitted by rule PostPublished for each attachment. A media item
        -- is attached to one post, once.
}

rule MediaReleased {
    when: ReleaseRequested(media)
    requires: media.status = attached
    ensures: media.status = purged

    @guidance
        -- Emitted when a post is withdrawn and when an edit names an
        -- attachment for removal (S14). The stored file goes with it.
}

-- Posts ------------------------------------------------------------------

rule PostPublished {
    when: PostSubmitted(author, caption, attachments, visibility, sensitive, spoiler_text, comments_disabled)
    requires: author.status = active
    requires: attachments.count > 0 and attachments.count <= config.max_album_length
    requires: attachments.all(m => m.owner = author and m.status = ready)
    requires: length_of(caption) <= config.max_caption_length
    requires: length_of(spoiler_text) <= config.max_spoiler_length
    ensures:
        let post = Post.created(author: author, caption: caption, visibility: visibility, sensitive: sensitive, spoiler_text: spoiler_text, comments_disabled: comments_disabled, published_at: now, edit_count: 0, status: published)
        for media in attachments:
            AttachRequested(media: media, post: post)
        FederationQueued(kind: create, from: author)

    @guidance
        -- A post needs media; a comment (rule CommentPublished) does not.
        -- Mentions in the caption notify the accounts mentioned; hashtags
        -- are indexed. A direct post is a DirectMessage, not a Post.
}

rule CommentPublished {
    when: CommentSubmitted(author, parent, text)
    requires: author.status = active
    requires: parent.status = published and not parent.comments_disabled
    requires: can_see(author, parent)
    requires: not exists Block{blocker: parent.author, blocked: author}
    requires: trimmed(text) != "" and length_of(text) <= config.max_caption_length
    ensures:
        let comment = Post.created(author: author, caption: text, visibility: parent.visibility, sensitive: false, spoiler_text: "", comments_disabled: false, in_reply_to: parent, thread_top: top_of(parent), published_at: now, edit_count: 0, status: published)
        if parent.author != author:
            Notification.created(recipient: parent.author, actor: author, kind: commented, post: parent, comment: comment, created_at: now, status: unread)
        FederationQueued(kind: create, from: author)

    @guidance
        -- top_of(p) is p for a post and p.thread_top for a comment. A
        -- comment carries no attachment: a request that names both a
        -- parent and an upload is refused, not published without the
        -- upload. A parent the author cannot read is answered exactly as
        -- one that does not exist. The one told is the author of what is
        -- answered, which for an answer to a comment is the commenter.
}

rule PostEdited {
    when: EditSubmitted(author, post, caption, sensitive, spoiler_text, removed)
    requires: post.author = author and author.status = active
    requires: post.status = published
    requires: post.edit_count < config.max_edits_per_post
    requires: length_of(caption) <= config.max_caption_length
    requires: removed.all(m => m.post = post)
    requires: post.is_comment or post.media.count - removed.count > 0
    ensures:
        post.caption = caption
        post.sensitive = sensitive
        post.spoiler_text = spoiler_text
        post.edit_count = post.edit_count + 1
        for media in removed:
            ReleaseRequested(media: media)
        FederationQueued(kind: update, from: author)

    @guidance
        -- S14. A field the request does not carry keeps its value, and an
        -- attachment leaves only when the request names it. The earlier
        -- text is kept as history the author and, for a public post,
        -- anyone can read.
}

rule PostWithdrawn {
    when: PostDeleteRequested(author, post)
    requires: post.author = author
    requires: post.status = published or post.status = taken_down
    ensures:
        post.status = withdrawn
        for media in post.media:
            ReleaseRequested(media: media)
        for like in post.likes:
            not exists like
        for share in post.shares:
            not exists share
        for bookmark in post.bookmarks:
            not exists bookmark
        for notice in post.notices:
            not exists notice
        for notice in post.notices_of_it:
            not exists notice
        FederationQueued(kind: delete, from: author)

    @guidance
        -- The author can always delete, including a post a moderator has
        -- taken down. This is also how a comment is deleted. What
        -- answered a deleted post or comment stays, as the posts of the
        -- people who wrote them (S22), and its notices go (S20).
}

rule PostTakenDown {
    when: action: ModerationAction.created
    requires: action.kind = remove_post
    requires: action.post != null
    let post = action.post
    requires: post.status = published
    ensures: post.status = taken_down

    @guidance
        -- A taken-down post is hidden from everyone but its author and
        -- the moderators, and is kept so that an appeal can restore it.
}

rule PostRestored {
    when: action: ModerationAction.status transitions_to reversed
    requires: action.kind = remove_post
    requires: action.post != null
    let post = action.post
    requires: post.status = taken_down
    ensures: post.status = published
}

-- Likes, shares, bookmarks -----------------------------------------------

rule PostLiked {
    when: LikeSubmitted(account, post)
    requires: account.status = active
    requires: post.status = published and can_see(account, post)
    requires: not exists Like{account: account, post: post}
    ensures:
        Like.created(account: account, post: post)
        if post.author != account:
            Notification.created(recipient: post.author, actor: account, kind: liked, post: post, created_at: now, status: unread)
        FederationQueued(kind: like, from: account)
}

rule PostUnliked {
    when: UnlikeSubmitted(account, post)
    let like = Like{account: account, post: post}
    let notice = Notification{actor: account, post: post, kind: liked}
    requires: exists like
    ensures:
        not exists like
        not exists notice
        FederationQueued(kind: undo, from: account)

    @guidance
        -- S20. Taking back a like that is not there changes nothing and
        -- is answered with the post, as liking twice is.
}

rule PostShared {
    when: ShareSubmitted(account, post)
    requires: account.status = active
    requires: post.status = published and post.visibility = public
    requires: not exists Block{blocker: post.author, blocked: account}
    requires: not exists Share{account: account, post: post}
    ensures:
        Share.created(account: account, post: post)
        if post.author != account:
            Notification.created(recipient: post.author, actor: account, kind: shared, post: post, created_at: now, status: unread)
        FederationQueued(kind: announce, from: account)

    @guidance
        -- The answer to the request carries the count after the share,
        -- not before it: counting is part of the rule, not a later job.
}

rule PostUnshared {
    when: UnshareSubmitted(account, post)
    let share = Share{account: account, post: post}
    requires: exists share
    ensures:
        not exists share
        FederationQueued(kind: undo, from: account)
}

rule PostBookmarked {
    when: BookmarkSubmitted(account, post)
    requires: post.status = published and can_see(account, post)
    requires: not exists Bookmark{account: account, post: post}
    ensures: Bookmark.created(account: account, post: post)

    @guidance
        -- A bookmark is private: it notifies nobody and is not federated.
}

rule PostUnbookmarked {
    when: UnbookmarkSubmitted(account, post)
    let bookmark = Bookmark{account: account, post: post}
    requires: exists bookmark
    ensures: not exists bookmark
}

-- Follows, blocks, mutes -------------------------------------------------

rule FollowedOpenAccount {
    when: FollowSubmitted(follower, target)
    requires: follower.status = active and target.status = active
    requires: follower != target and not target.locked
    requires: not exists Follow{follower: follower, target: target}
    requires: not exists Block{blocker: target, blocked: follower}
    requires: not exists Block{blocker: follower, blocked: target}
    ensures:
        Follow.created(follower: follower, target: target, status: following)
        Notification.created(recipient: target, actor: follower, kind: followed, created_at: now, status: unread)
        FederationQueued(kind: follow, from: follower)
}

rule FollowRequestedOfLockedAccount {
    when: FollowSubmitted(follower, target)
    requires: follower.status = active and target.status = active
    requires: follower != target and target.locked
    requires: not exists Follow{follower: follower, target: target}
    requires: not exists Block{blocker: target, blocked: follower}
    requires: not exists Block{blocker: follower, blocked: target}
    ensures:
        Follow.created(follower: follower, target: target, status: requested)
        Notification.created(recipient: target, actor: follower, kind: follow_requested, created_at: now, status: unread)
        FederationQueued(kind: follow, from: follower)
}

rule FollowRequestAccepted {
    when: FollowRequestAccepted(target, follow)
    requires: follow.target = target
    requires: follow.status = requested
    ensures:
        follow.status = following
        FederationQueued(kind: accept, from: target)
}

rule FollowRequestRejected {
    when: FollowRequestRejected(target, follow)
    requires: follow.target = target
    requires: follow.status = requested
    ensures:
        not exists follow
        FederationQueued(kind: reject, from: target)
}

rule Unfollowed {
    when: UnfollowSubmitted(follower, target)
    let follow = Follow{follower: follower, target: target}
    let notice = Notification{recipient: target, actor: follower, kind: followed}
    let request_notice = Notification{recipient: target, actor: follower, kind: follow_requested}
    requires: exists follow
    ensures:
        not exists follow
        not exists notice
        not exists request_notice
        FederationQueued(kind: undo, from: follower)

    @guidance
        -- Also how a pending request is withdrawn. The notice of the
        -- follow goes with it (S20).
}

rule AccountBlocked {
    when: BlockSubmitted(blocker, blocked)
    requires: blocker != blocked
    requires: not exists Block{blocker: blocker, blocked: blocked}
    let outgoing = Follow{follower: blocker, target: blocked}
    let incoming = Follow{follower: blocked, target: blocker}
    ensures:
        Block.created(blocker: blocker, blocked: blocked)
        not exists outgoing
        not exists incoming
        FederationQueued(kind: block, from: blocker)

    @guidance
        -- A moderator can be blocked like anyone else. Pixelfed refuses to
        -- let an admin be blocked; a moderator's notices still arrive,
        -- because they come from the instance and not from the person.
}

rule AccountUnblocked {
    when: UnblockSubmitted(blocker, blocked)
    let block = Block{blocker: blocker, blocked: blocked}
    requires: exists block
    ensures:
        not exists block
        FederationQueued(kind: undo, from: blocker)
}

rule AccountMuted {
    when: MuteSubmitted(muter, muted)
    requires: muter != muted
    requires: not exists Mute{muter: muter, muted: muted}
    ensures: Mute.created(muter: muter, muted: muted)

    @guidance
        -- A mute is private: the muted account is never told and nothing
        -- is federated.
}

rule AccountUnmuted {
    when: UnmuteSubmitted(muter, muted)
    let mute = Mute{muter: muter, muted: muted}
    requires: exists mute
    ensures: not exists mute
}

rule HashtagFollowed {
    when: HashtagFollowSubmitted(account, hashtag)
    requires: not hashtag.banned
    requires: not exists HashtagFollow{account: account, hashtag: hashtag}
    ensures: HashtagFollow.created(account: account, hashtag: hashtag)

    @guidance
        -- A tag nobody has used yet can be followed; Pixelfed answers 422.
}

rule HashtagUnfollowed {
    when: HashtagUnfollowSubmitted(account, hashtag)
    let followed = HashtagFollow{account: account, hashtag: hashtag}
    requires: exists followed
    ensures: not exists followed
}

rule NotificationSeen {
    when: NotificationsRead(recipient, notification)
    requires: notification.recipient = recipient
    requires: notification.status = unread
    ensures: notification.status = seen

    @guidance
        -- Raised for every notification on a page when the page is read
        -- (S20). The post sent beside a notification obeys the reading
        -- rules: one the recipient can no longer read is left out and
        -- the notification is sent without it.
}

-- Direct messages --------------------------------------------------------

rule MessageSent {
    when: MessageSubmitted(sender, recipient, text)
    requires: sender.status = active and recipient.status = active
    requires: sender != recipient
    requires: trimmed(text) != "" and length_of(text) <= config.max_message_length
    requires: not exists Block{blocker: recipient, blocked: sender}
    requires: not exists Block{blocker: sender, blocked: recipient}
    ensures:
        DirectMessage.created(sender: sender, recipient: recipient, text: text, sent_at: now, status: sent)
        Notification.created(recipient: recipient, actor: sender, kind: message_received, created_at: now, status: unread)

    @guidance
        -- A message from someone the recipient does not follow arrives as
        -- a request the recipient accepts or ignores. To a remote
        -- recipient the message is delivered to that one inbox only.
}

rule MessageUnsent {
    when: MessageDeleteRequested(sender, message)
    requires: message.sender = sender
    requires: message.status = sent
    ensures: message.status = unsent
}

-- Reports and moderation -------------------------------------------------

rule ReportFiled {
    when: ReportSubmitted(reporter, reason, note, about_account, about_post, about_message)
    requires: reporter.status = active
    requires: about_account != reporter
    requires: length_of(note) <= config.max_report_note_length
    requires: about_message = null or about_message.recipient = reporter or about_message.sender = reporter
    ensures:
        Report.created(reporter: reporter, reason: reason, note: note, about_account: about_account, about_post: about_post, about_message: about_message, filed_at: now, status: filed)
        if not about_account.is_local:
            FederationQueued(kind: flag, from: reporter)

    @guidance
        -- A report about a direct message can only come from one of its
        -- two participants, and it is what lets a moderator read that
        -- message (S15). The reported account is not told who reported.
}

rule ReportDismissed {
    when: ReportDismissed(moderator, report, reason)
    requires: moderator.is_moderator and moderator.status = active
    requires: report.status = filed
    ensures:
        report.status = dismissed
        AuditEntry.created(actor: moderator, what: reason, at: now)
}

rule ActionTaken {
    when: ActionDecided(moderator, kind, subject, post, rule_cited, reason, report)
    requires: moderator.is_moderator and moderator.status = active
    requires: moderator != subject
    requires: trimmed(reason) != ""
    requires: report = null or report.status = filed
    ensures:
        ModerationAction.created(kind: kind, subject: subject, post: post, moderator: moderator, rule_cited: rule_cited, reason: reason, report: report, taken_at: now, status: applied)
        Notification.created(recipient: subject, kind: moderation_notice, post: post, created_at: now, status: unread)
        AuditEntry.created(actor: moderator, what: reason, at: now)
        if report != null:
            ReportClosed(report: report)

    @guidance
        -- S5. The action and its notice are one entity, so one cannot be
        -- written without the other; the notification is how the notice
        -- reaches the person. A moderator cannot act on their own account.
        -- limit_reach and mark_sensitive take effect through the reading
        -- rules (invariants below), not through a status of their own.
}

rule ReportActioned {
    when: ReportClosed(report)
    requires: report.status = filed
    ensures: report.status = actioned
}

rule AppealFiled {
    when: AppealSubmitted(subject, action, text)
    requires: action.subject = subject
    requires: action.status = applied
    requires: trimmed(text) != ""
    ensures:
        action.status = under_appeal
        action.appeal_text = text

    @guidance
        -- S6. One appeal per action. The action stays in force while the
        -- appeal is open; a suspended account can file one, since filing
        -- needs only a session.
}

rule AppealUpheld {
    when: AppealDecided(reviewer, action, grant)
    requires: reviewer.is_moderator and reviewer.status = active
    requires: reviewer != action.moderator and reviewer != action.subject
    requires: action.status = under_appeal
    requires: not grant
    ensures:
        action.status = upheld
        action.decided_by = reviewer
        Notification.created(recipient: action.subject, kind: moderation_notice, post: action.post, created_at: now, status: unread)
        AuditEntry.created(actor: reviewer, what: "appeal upheld", at: now)
}

rule AppealGranted {
    when: AppealDecided(reviewer, action, grant)
    requires: reviewer.is_moderator and reviewer.status = active
    requires: reviewer != action.moderator and reviewer != action.subject
    requires: action.status = under_appeal
    requires: grant
    ensures:
        action.status = reversed
        action.decided_by = reviewer
        Notification.created(recipient: action.subject, kind: moderation_notice, post: action.post, created_at: now, status: unread)
        AuditEntry.created(actor: reviewer, what: "appeal granted", at: now)

    @guidance
        -- Reversal undoes the action's effect: rules AccountReinstated
        -- and PostRestored fire on it.
}

rule DomainBlocked {
    when: DomainBlockDecided(moderator, domain, reason)
    requires: moderator.is_moderator and moderator.status = active
    requires: trimmed(reason) != ""
    requires: not exists DomainBlock{domain: domain}
    ensures:
        DomainBlock.created(domain: domain, reason: reason, blocked_by: moderator)
        AuditEntry.created(actor: moderator, what: reason, at: now)

    @guidance
        -- S7. The list and each reason are public. People who follow
        -- accounts on the domain are told before the follows are cut.
}

-- Federation -------------------------------------------------------------

rule DeliveriesQueued {
    when: FederationQueued(kind, from)
    requires: from.is_local
    ensures:
        for inbox in inboxes_addressed(kind, from):
            Delivery.created(kind: kind, from: from, inbox: inbox, attempts: 0, next_attempt_at: now, status: queued)

    @guidance
        -- inboxes_addressed is the audience of the activity and nothing
        -- wider (contract ActivityPub, AddressedOnly): shared inboxes are
        -- used where a server offers one, blocked domains are left out.
}

rule DeliverySucceeded {
    when: DeliveryAnswered(_, delivery, accepted)
    requires: delivery.status = queued
    requires: accepted
    ensures: delivery.status = delivered
}

rule DeliveryRefused {
    when: DeliveryAnswered(_, delivery, accepted)
    requires: delivery.status = queued
    requires: not accepted
    ensures:
        delivery.status = backing_off
        delivery.attempts = delivery.attempts + 1
        delivery.next_attempt_at = now + backoff_after(delivery.attempts)
}

rule DeliveryRetried {
    when: delivery: Delivery.next_attempt_at <= now
    requires: delivery.status = backing_off
    requires: delivery.attempts < config.delivery_max_attempts
    ensures: delivery.status = queued
}

rule DeliveryAbandoned {
    when: delivery: Delivery.next_attempt_at <= now
    requires: delivery.status = backing_off
    requires: delivery.attempts >= config.delivery_max_attempts
    ensures: delivery.status = abandoned

    @guidance
        -- backoff_after doubles from delivery_first_backoff. A server that
        -- has refused everything for a week is marked unreachable and
        -- probed daily rather than sent every activity.
}

rule InboundArrived {
    when: ActivityReceived(origin, kind, actor_uri)
    ensures: InboundActivity.created(kind: kind, origin: origin, actor_uri: actor_uri, status: awaiting_verification)
}

rule InboundAccepted {
    when: SignatureChecked(inbound, valid)
    requires: inbound.status = awaiting_verification
    requires: valid
    requires: exists RemoteServer{domain: inbound.origin.domain}
    requires: not exists DomainBlock{domain: inbound.origin.domain}
    ensures: inbound.status = accepted

    @guidance
        -- An accepted activity is applied through the same rules a local
        -- request goes through, with the remote account as the actor, so
        -- a block or a locked account means the same to both.
}

rule InboundRefused {
    when: SignatureChecked(inbound, valid)
    requires: inbound.status = awaiting_verification
    requires: not valid or exists DomainBlock{domain: inbound.origin.domain}
    ensures: inbound.status = refused
}

-- Export -----------------------------------------------------------------

rule ExportRequested {
    when: ExportRequested(account)
    requires: account.status != departed
    ensures: Export.created(account: account, requested_at: now, status: asked)

    @guidance
        -- S8. Not refused to a suspended or a leaving account.
}

rule ExportBuilt {
    when: ExportFinished(export)
    requires: export.status = asked
    ensures:
        export.status = built
        export.built_at = now
}

rule ExportCleared {
    when: export: Export.built_at + config.export_lifetime <= now
    requires: export.status = built
    ensures:
        export.status = cleared
        export.built_at = null
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant OneLikePerAccountAndPost {
    for a in Likes:
        for b in Likes:
            a != b implies a.account != b.account or a.post != b.post
}

invariant CommentsNameTheirThread {
    for p in Posts:
        p.is_comment = (p.thread_top != null)
}

invariant NobodyIsToldOfTheirOwnAct {
    for n in Notifications:
        n.actor != n.recipient
}

invariant OneNoticePerLike {
    for a in Notifications:
        for b in Notifications:
            a != b and a.kind = liked and b.kind = liked implies a.actor != b.actor or a.post != b.post
}

invariant OneNoticePerFollow {
    for a in Notifications:
        for b in Notifications:
            a != b and (a.kind = followed or a.kind = follow_requested) and (b.kind = followed or b.kind = follow_requested) implies a.actor != b.actor or a.recipient != b.recipient
}

invariant OneShareOfPublicPostsOnly {
    for s in Shares:
        s.post.visibility = public
}

invariant OneFollowPerPair {
    for a in Follows:
        for b in Follows:
            a != b implies a.follower != b.follower or a.target != b.target
}

invariant NobodyFollowsThemselves {
    for f in Follows:
        f.follower != f.target
}

invariant NoFollowAcrossABlock {
    for b in Blocks:
        not exists Follow{follower: b.blocker, target: b.blocked}
        and not exists Follow{follower: b.blocked, target: b.blocker}
}

invariant AttachedMediaBelongsToItsPostsAuthor {
    for m in Media:
        m.status = attached implies m.post != null and m.post.author = m.owner
}

invariant PostsHaveMediaAndCommentsNeedNone {
    for p in Posts:
        p.status = published and not p.is_comment implies p.media.count > 0
}

invariant EditsAreBounded {
    for p in Posts:
        p.edit_count <= config.max_edits_per_post
}

invariant PublicClientsAlwaysUsePkce {
    for c in AuthorizationCodes:
        c.client.kind = public_client implies c.pkce != null
}

invariant PublicClientsHoldNoSecret {
    for c in OAuthClients:
        c.kind = public_client implies c.secret_hash = null
}

invariant NoActionWithoutAReason {
    -- S5.
    for a in ModerationActions:
        a.reason != ""
}

invariant NobodyModeratesThemselves {
    for a in ModerationActions:
        a.moderator != a.subject
}

invariant AppealsAreDecidedBySomeoneElse {
    -- S6.
    for a in ModerationActions:
        a.status in { upheld, reversed } implies a.decided_by != null and a.decided_by != a.moderator
}

invariant DepartedAccountsHoldNothing {
    -- S9.
    for a in Accounts:
        a.status = departed implies
            (a.posts where status = published).count = 0
            and a.followers.count = 0
            and a.following.count = 0
            and (a.tokens where status = valid).count = 0
}

-- Reading rules. Who may see what is a property of every read, not of an
-- entity's state, so it is stated here and demanded of surface ClientApi:
--
--   can_see(viewer, post)   the post is published, and: it is public or
--                           unlisted; or it is followers_only and viewer
--                           is its author or an accepted follower; and
--                           neither of viewer and author blocks the
--                           other. A taken_down post is seen by its
--                           author and by moderators only. A published
--                           comment is seen by its author and by whoever
--                           can see the post at the top of its thread
--                           (S22); the comment's own author's followers
--                           have no part in it.
--   a thread                what a post answers, from the top down, and
--                           the published comments under it at any
--                           depth, oldest first, config.context_max of
--                           them at most. A reader who sees a comment of
--                           their own under a post they can no longer
--                           see is shown their own part and no more.
--   the lists of likes      an account's likes and its bookmarks, newest
--   and bookmarks           first by when each was placed, hold only what
--                           the account can still see.
--   home timeline           the viewer's own published posts, and
--                           those of accounts the viewer follows and of
--                           hashtags the viewer follows that the viewer
--                           can see, minus muted accounts, newest first,
--                           nothing else (S10). Comments are not in it.
--   public timeline         public posts by local accounts that are not
--                           under an applied limit_reach action.
--   limit_reach             keeps an account's posts out of the public
--                           timeline, hashtag feeds and trending lists.
--                           Followers still see them and the account is
--                           told (S5): this is the only form of reduced
--                           reach there is.
--   mark_sensitive          the post is served with sensitive true.
--   trending                local public posts of the range ordered by
--                           likes, by a rule the about page states.
--   direct messages         readable by sender and recipient; by a
--                           moderator only for a message named in a
--                           report filed by a participant (S15).

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

actor Member {
    identified_by: Account where status = active or status = suspended or status = leaving
}

actor Moderator {
    identified_by: Account where is_moderator and status = active
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Before there is a session: registration, the consent page, the token
-- endpoint.
surface SignIn {
    facing client: OAuthClient

    exposes:
        client.name
        client.kind
        client.redirect_uris
        client.scopes
        client.codes.count
        config.open_registration

    provides:
        RegistrationSubmitted(client, username, password) when config.open_registration
        ClientRegistrationSubmitted(client, name, kind, redirect_uris, scopes)
        CodePresented(client, code, redirect_uri, verifier, secret)

    @guarantee SecretsAreNeverReturnedTwice
        -- A client secret is shown at registration and stored hashed; a
        -- password is never stored or logged in a form that can be read.

    @guarantee TheFrontAddressAnswersAPerson
        -- GET / is a page that says the server is running, that it has
        -- no website, and which address to give the app, in the form the
        -- app takes it. It asks for nothing and reads nothing from the
        -- database. Until 2026-11-12 the address answered the
        -- missing-page error, and on winsmuth that day a person who
        -- opened it in a browser took the server for broken. The sign-in
        -- form is reached only through the link the app opens, because
        -- the form is made from the app's authorization request.
}

-- The client API with a token (contract ClientApiCompat).
surface ClientApi {
    facing member: Member

    exposes:
        member.username
        member.display_name
        member.note
        member.locked
        member.status
        member.moved_to
        member.is_local
        member.accepted_followers.count
        member.blocks.count
        for post in member.posts:
            post.caption
            post.visibility
            post.sensitive
            post.spoiler_text
            post.comments_disabled
            post.published_at
            post.edit_count
            post.status
            post.likes_count
            post.shares_count
            post.reply_count
        for token in member.tokens:
            token.scopes
            token.issued_at
            token.status
        for notice in member.notices:
            notice.kind
            notice.rule_cited
            notice.reason
            notice.taken_at
            notice.status
            notice.appeal_text

    provides:
        ConsentGiven(member, client, redirect_uri, scopes, pkce)
        RevocationRequested(member, token)
        UploadSubmitted(member, mime, size_bytes) when member.status = active
        MediaDeleteRequested(member, media)
        PostSubmitted(member, caption, attachments, visibility, sensitive, spoiler_text, comments_disabled) when member.status = active
        CommentSubmitted(member, parent, text) when member.status = active
        EditSubmitted(member, post, caption, sensitive, spoiler_text, removed) when member.status = active
        PostDeleteRequested(member, post)
        LikeSubmitted(member, post) when member.status = active
        UnlikeSubmitted(member, post)
        ShareSubmitted(member, post) when member.status = active
        UnshareSubmitted(member, post)
        BookmarkSubmitted(member, post)
        UnbookmarkSubmitted(member, post)
        FollowSubmitted(member, target) when member.status = active
        FollowRequestAccepted(member, follow)
        FollowRequestRejected(member, follow)
        UnfollowSubmitted(member, target)
        BlockSubmitted(member, blocked)
        UnblockSubmitted(member, blocked)
        MuteSubmitted(member, muted)
        UnmuteSubmitted(member, muted)
        HashtagFollowSubmitted(member, hashtag)
        HashtagUnfollowSubmitted(member, hashtag)
        NotificationsRead(member, notification)
        MessageSubmitted(member, recipient, text) when member.status = active
        MessageDeleteRequested(member, message)
        ReportSubmitted(member, reason, note, about_account, about_post, about_message) when member.status = active
        AppealSubmitted(member, action, text)
        ExportRequested(member)
        MoveRequested(member, destination)
        DeletionRequested(member)
        DeletionWithdrawn(member) when member.status = leaving

    contracts:
        fulfils ClientApiCompat

    @guarantee SuspensionLeavesTheWayOut
        -- A suspended account cannot post, comment, like, share, follow,
        -- message or report. It can still read its notices, appeal,
        -- export, move, delete its posts and delete itself (S8, S9).

    @guarantee ReadsObeyTheReadingRules
        -- No route returns a post the viewer cannot see under can_see,
        -- whichever list, search or notification it would arrive in.

    @guarantee NothingIsInsertedIntoAFeed
        -- S10.
}

surface ModerationDesk {
    facing moderator: Moderator

    exposes:
        moderator.username
        for report in Reports where status = filed:
            report.reason
            report.note
            report.filed_at
            report.status
        for entry in AuditEntries:
            entry.actor
            entry.what
            entry.at
        for blocked in DomainBlocks:
            blocked.domain
            blocked.reason
            blocked.blocked_by

    provides:
        ReportDismissed(moderator, report, reason)
        ActionDecided(moderator, kind, subject, post, rule_cited, reason, report)
        AppealDecided(moderator, action, grant)
        DomainBlockDecided(moderator, domain, reason)

    @guarantee NoSilentActions
        -- S5. There is no control here that changes what an account or a
        -- post can reach without rule ActionTaken, and so without a
        -- notice.

    @guarantee MessagesStayPrivate
        -- S15. No list, search or lookup on this surface returns a direct
        -- message that is not named in an open report by a participant.

    @guarantee EverythingIsLogged
        -- Every provided operation writes an AuditEntry.
}

-- What anyone can read without an account (S7).
surface PublicRecord {
    facing reader: RemoteServer

    exposes:
        reader.domain
        for blocked in DomainBlocks:
            blocked.domain
            blocked.reason
        (ModerationActions where status = applied).count
        (ModerationActions where status = reversed).count

    @guarantee NobodyIsNamed
        -- Counts by kind and month, and blocked domains with reasons. No
        -- account, post or report appears.
}

-- Other servers.
surface Federation {
    facing remote: RemoteServer

    exposes:
        remote.domain
        remote.shared_inbox
        for delivery in Deliveries:
            delivery.kind
            delivery.inbox
            delivery.attempts
            delivery.next_attempt_at
            delivery.status

    provides:
        ActivityReceived(remote, kind, actor_uri)
        DeliveryAnswered(remote, delivery, accepted)

    contracts:
        fulfils ActivityPub

    @guarantee NothingBeyondTheAudience
        -- S16.
}

-- The server's own workers: media processing, signature checks, exports.
surface Workers {
    facing worker: Account

    exposes:
        worker.is_moderator
        for media in Media:
            media.mime
            media.size_bytes
            media.alt_text
            media.status
        for inbound in InboundActivities:
            inbound.kind
            inbound.actor_uri
            inbound.status
        for export in Exports:
            export.requested_at
            export.status

    provides:
        ProcessingFinished(media)
        ProcessingFailed(media)
        SignatureChecked(inbound, valid)
        ExportFinished(export)

    @guidance
        -- These are internal completions, modelled as a surface so that
        -- every trigger has a source. The facing account stands for the
        -- instance's own actor.
}

-- The repository as the person who runs the server meets it.
surface OperatorShell {
    facing operator: Account

    exposes:
        operator.username
        for issue in KnownIssues where status = open:
            issue.name
            issue.effect
            issue.closes_when

    @guidance
        -- pellucid-server serve applies migrations and listens, on this
        -- machine only by default, for a reverse proxy to reach.
        -- pellucid-server migrate applies migrations and stops.
        -- pellucid-server create-account NAME [--moderator] is rule
        -- AccountRegistered for an operator; the password is read from
        -- standard input and is at least twelve characters. Settings come
        -- from flags or from PELLUCID_DATABASE_URL, PELLUCID_BASE_URL,
        -- PELLUCID_TITLE, PELLUCID_MEDIA_DIR, PELLUCID_HOST and
        -- PELLUCID_PORT. Development: nix develop, cabal build all,
        -- cabal test all, fish scripts/check.fish. On a machine that
        -- runs the NixOS module, pellucid-server-manage takes the same
        -- commands; it is run as root and runs them as the service's
        -- user with the service's settings.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred ActivityPub.protocol          -- see: https://www.w3.org/TR/activitypub/ and https://docs.joinmastodon.org/spec/activitypub/
deferred HttpSignatures.draft          -- see: draft-cavage-http-signatures-12 and RFC 9421
deferred OAuth2.pkce                   -- see: RFC 6749, RFC 7636, RFC 7009
deferred Pixelfed.client_api           -- see: pellucid.allium contracts PixelfedApi and Pagers
deferred Stories.lifecycle             -- see: not written; Pixelfed's app/Http/Controllers/Stories
deferred Collections.lifecycle         -- see: not written; Pixelfed's /api/v1.1/collections

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Whether decisions S5 to S16 are what less authoritarian means. They are a reading of the phrase, written down so it can be corrected; each one that is wrong should be struck before any code depends on it."
open question "How previews and blurhashes are made under S19. A smaller rendition needs the picture decoded, and a decoder is the largest attack surface a media server has. The candidates are a decoder in a separate process with no network, no filesystem and a memory limit, or accepting full-size previews and making none."
open question "Whether S20 to S22 are right. S21 in particular makes a choice Pixelfed did not: everyone who can read a post can page through everyone who likes it."
open question "Whether a post's reply_count should count its whole thread. It counts direct answers, as the entity says, so a post whose only comment was deleted shows 0 while its thread still holds what answered that comment."
open question "What a suspension does to the posts the account already made. The rules say what a suspended account cannot do and nothing about whether its posts stay in timelines and on its profile. The code follows the rules as written: they stay."
open question "How sign-in attempts are limited (KnownIssue no_sign_in_throttle) without turning the limit into a way to lock a person out of their own account by guessing at it."
open question "Whether the client API should stay Pixelfed-compatible indefinitely or only until Pellucid's own client is the main one. Compatibility is S1; it also fixes the entity shapes, the four historical pagination parameters and the _pe flag in place."
open question "Whether direct messages should be end-to-end encrypted between Pellucid servers, which S15 would then enforce by construction, and what is shown to a recipient on a server that cannot decrypt."
open question "How an instance with a single moderator satisfies S6. The appeal can be recorded and answered, but not by someone else; a shared appeals pool between cooperating instances is one answer."
open question "Whether trending lists should exist at all under S10, or whether discovery is hashtags and search only."
open question "What stories, collections and groups look like under these decisions. They are deferred, not rejected."
